{"schemaVersion":1,"generatedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","id":"912656e4dd362ad9903867a9","canonicalUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260814141724.1006382-1-daniel.baluta%40nxp.com/","channels":["linux-arm-msm"],"thread":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"thread:lore-git:20260814141724.1006382-1-daniel.baluta@nxp.com","source":{"kind":"static-generated","canonicalThreadUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260814141724.1006382-1-daniel.baluta%40nxp.com/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","contentDigest":"lore-git:20260814141724.1006382-1-daniel.baluta@nxp.com"},"subject":"[PATCH v5 0/3] soc: qcom: ubwc: Fix link error when QCOM_SMEM=n","messages":{"20260814141724.1006382-1-daniel.baluta@nxp.com":{"id":"20260814141724.1006382-1-daniel.baluta@nxp.com","messageId":"20260814141724.1006382-1-daniel.baluta@nxp.com","references":[],"missingAncestorIds":[],"author":{"name":"Daniel Baluta","address":"daniel.baluta@nxp.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"","address":"andersson@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"konradybcio@kernel.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"","address":"dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-msm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"nathan@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"imx@lists.linux.dev"},{"name":"Daniel Baluta","address":"daniel.baluta@nxp.com"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-14T14:17:21.000Z","iso":"2026-08-14T14:17:21.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"[PATCH v5 0/3] soc: qcom: ubwc: Fix link error when QCOM_SMEM=n","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-arm-msm.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-arm-msm.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"DRM_MSM and VIDEO_QCOM_IRIS select QCOM_UBWC_CONFIG, whose\nubwc_config.c calls QCOM_SMEM APIs unconditionally. On configs without\nQCOM_SMEM this fails to link, e.g. on SOC_IMX5:"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"  arm-linux-gnueabihf-ld: ubwc_config.c:(.text+0x2c): undefined"},{"kind":"code","text":"      reference to 'qcom_smem_is_available'"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Fix it by making the QCOM_SMEM requirement explicit in Kconfig."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Changes since v4: (fixed coments from sashiko bot)\n- Dropped the IS_REACHABLE() patch. As pointed out in review, it did not\n  fix the case where DRM_MSM=y and QCOM_SMEM=m. it only masked the mismatch\n  at build time and turned it into a guaranteed runtime probe failure,\n  since all callers abort when qcom_ubwc_config_get_data() returns an\n  error. Instead the mismatch is now made unconfigurable with\n  'depends on QCOM_SMEM || QCOM_SMEM=n' on both drivers, so the header\n  keeps the plain IS_ENABLED() test.\n- Reordered so the selects are guarded first and the QCOM_SMEM\n  dependency is added to QCOM_UBWC_CONFIG last so that we dont break\n  bisection as pointed by Nathan"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Link to v4:\n  - https://lore.kernel.org/imx/20260812151934.709198-1-daniel.baluta@nxp.com/"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Daniel Baluta (3):\n  drm/msm: Guard the QCOM_UBWC_CONFIG select with QCOM_SMEM\n  media: iris: Guard the QCOM_UBWC_CONFIG select with QCOM_SMEM\n  soc: qcom: ubwc: Fix link error when QCOM_SMEM=n"},{"kind":"code","text":" drivers/gpu/drm/msm/Kconfig              | 3 ++-"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":" drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/Kconfig | 3 ++-"},{"kind":"code","text":" drivers/soc/qcom/Kconfig                 | 1 +"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":" 3 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)"},{"kind":"signature","text":"2.45.2","lineCount":1}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":0,"diagnostics":[]},"20260814141724.1006382-2-daniel.baluta@nxp.com":{"id":"20260814141724.1006382-2-daniel.baluta@nxp.com","messageId":"20260814141724.1006382-2-daniel.baluta@nxp.com","references":["20260814141724.1006382-1-daniel.baluta@nxp.com"],"missingAncestorIds":[],"author":{"name":"Daniel Baluta","address":"daniel.baluta@nxp.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"","address":"andersson@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"konradybcio@kernel.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"","address":"dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-msm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"nathan@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"imx@lists.linux.dev"},{"name":"Daniel Baluta","address":"daniel.baluta@nxp.com"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-14T14:17:22.000Z","iso":"2026-08-14T14:17:22.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"[PATCH v5 1/3] drm/msm: Guard the QCOM_UBWC_CONFIG select with QCOM_SMEM","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-arm-msm.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-arm-msm.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"QCOM_UBWC_CONFIG is about to depend on QCOM_SMEM. Guard the DRM_MSM\nselect with 'if ARCH_QCOM && QCOM_SMEM', and add\n'depends on QCOM_SMEM || QCOM_SMEM=n' so a built-in driver is never\nselected against a missing or modular SMEM."},{"kind":"code","text":"Fixes: 1b445022d1d0 (\"soc: qcom: ubwc: Get HBB from SMEM\")"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Signed-off-by: Daniel Baluta <daniel.baluta@nxp.com>"},{"kind":"patch","patchId":"patch:20260814141724.1006382-2-daniel.baluta@nxp.com:1:0"}],"patchIds":["patch:20260814141724.1006382-2-daniel.baluta@nxp.com:1:0"],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":1,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260814141724.1006382-1-daniel.baluta@nxp.com","parentId":"20260814141724.1006382-1-daniel.baluta@nxp.com"},"20260814141724.1006382-3-daniel.baluta@nxp.com":{"id":"20260814141724.1006382-3-daniel.baluta@nxp.com","messageId":"20260814141724.1006382-3-daniel.baluta@nxp.com","references":["20260814141724.1006382-1-daniel.baluta@nxp.com"],"missingAncestorIds":[],"author":{"name":"Daniel Baluta","address":"daniel.baluta@nxp.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"","address":"andersson@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"konradybcio@kernel.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"","address":"dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-msm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"nathan@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"imx@lists.linux.dev"},{"name":"Daniel Baluta","address":"daniel.baluta@nxp.com"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-14T14:17:23.000Z","iso":"2026-08-14T14:17:23.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"[PATCH v5 2/3] media: iris: Guard the QCOM_UBWC_CONFIG select with QCOM_SMEM","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-arm-msm.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-arm-msm.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"QCOM_UBWC_CONFIG is about to depend on QCOM_SMEM. Guard the\nVIDEO_QCOM_IRIS select with 'if ARCH_QCOM && QCOM_SMEM', and add\n'depends on QCOM_SMEM || QCOM_SMEM=n' so a built-in driver is never\nselected against a missing or modular SMEM."},{"kind":"code","text":"Fixes: c43207553867 (\"media: iris: retrieve UBWC platform configuration\")"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Signed-off-by: Daniel Baluta <daniel.baluta@nxp.com>"},{"kind":"patch","patchId":"patch:20260814141724.1006382-3-daniel.baluta@nxp.com:2:0"}],"patchIds":["patch:20260814141724.1006382-3-daniel.baluta@nxp.com:2:0"],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":2,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260814141724.1006382-1-daniel.baluta@nxp.com","parentId":"20260814141724.1006382-1-daniel.baluta@nxp.com"},"20260814141724.1006382-4-daniel.baluta@nxp.com":{"id":"20260814141724.1006382-4-daniel.baluta@nxp.com","messageId":"20260814141724.1006382-4-daniel.baluta@nxp.com","references":["20260814141724.1006382-1-daniel.baluta@nxp.com"],"missingAncestorIds":[],"author":{"name":"Daniel Baluta","address":"daniel.baluta@nxp.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"","address":"andersson@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"konradybcio@kernel.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"","address":"dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-msm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"nathan@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"imx@lists.linux.dev"},{"name":"Daniel Baluta","address":"